# Copy this file to .env.local and fill in your own key. .env.local is
# gitignored and never committed.
#
# Get a free Gemini API key at https://aistudio.google.com/apikey
#
# Without this key, Onclave runs exactly as it does today: Community, Food
# Near You, Cultural Places, and Events all work fully on the local demo
# dataset. With it, each of those pages also shows a "Live results" section
# powered by Gemini with Google Search grounding, so results can include
# real, current communities, restaurants, places, and events beyond the demo
# data — clearly labeled and separate from it.
GEMINI_API_KEY=

# Optional: override the Gemini model used for live search. Defaults to
# gemini-3.6-flash if unset.
#
# Note: Google Search grounding (what this feature relies on) draws from a
# separate quota than plain generation and, on some accounts, requires
# billing to be enabled on the linked Google Cloud project even to use the
# free tier. If live results silently don't appear, check usage/billing at
# https://ai.dev/rate-limit for the project tied to your key.
GEMINI_MODEL=

# Optional backup provider. When GEMINI_API_KEY is missing, hits its quota,
# or errors, both /api/live-search and /api/ai-generate automatically retry
# with Groq instead of failing outright. Not required if Gemini alone is
# enough for your use case.
#
# Get a free Groq API key at https://console.groq.com/keys
GROQ_API_KEY=

# Optional: override the Groq model. Defaults to openai/gpt-oss-120b. See
# https://console.groq.com/docs/models for currently available models —
# Groq's lineup changes over time and old model ids can 404.
GROQ_MODEL=
